    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the **Austin Waves** prioritizes efficiency against favorable pitching matchups, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.26) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.68). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Scott and a prime #2 order slot, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high xwOBA (0.377) and a favorable park shift against Weathers. **Josh Jung** (66.28) and **Kyle Tucker** (65.46) round out our most potent offensive threats; **Josh Jung** is a standout play today, as the 5.33 xERA of Quintana combined with park factors and a projected #3 spot creates an elite environment for run production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Nolan Schanuel**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a respectable 51.46 projection. While **Nolan Schanuel** benefits from a slight park boost and wind out in his matchup against Ginn, the optimizer favored the higher volatility/ceiling of **Dominic Smith** and **Jackson Merrill** to maintain our aggressive pursuit of SB potential. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Josh Jung**, **Josh Lowe**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill** closely; if any of these players move down the batting order, their efficiency scores will adjust downward significantly. We remain cautious with **Gunnar Henderson** (48.95) today; while his speed is an asset, facing a high-skill arm like McClanahan and dealing with a significant negative platoon split forces us to treat him as a marginal start. We continue to hold **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, awaiting his return to bolster our overall scoring floor.",
